  "id": "COMPOUND:16884 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "Dieckol is implicated in the regulation of CCF-STTG1 through a multi-step pathway involving the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. This transporter is targeted by both Dieckol and other compounds, such as Michaolide J and (-)-Duryne F, which in turn target CCF-STTG1. The evidence suggests that Dieckol may modulate the activity of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, potentially influencing the function of CCF-STTG1. The integration of these pathways implies that Dieckol could exert its effects on CCF-STTG1 through a mechanism involving the transporter, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores and the shared target relationship across different compounds support a plausible link between Dieckol and CCF-STTG1, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the mechanistic details.",
